<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">25022026</say-as>.</s>
<s>The eighth of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s>
<s>It's morning in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, just after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fædʒɚ">Fajr</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Forensic Architecture, a British research group, found that Israeli soldiers fired nine hundred and ten bullets in under six minutes at <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɑl ɑl sʊlˈtɑn">Tal al-Sultan</phoneme> last March, killing fifteen medics — striking marked aid vehicles first, then shooting survivors at close range.</s>
<s>Satellite imagery confirmed that Israeli bulldozers buried the wreckage afterwards, and earthen berms were raised to conceal the site.</s>
<s>As the findings reached the public, Israel separately ordered thirty-seven aid organizations to halt all operations in Gaza and the West Bank — a directive rights groups are now challenging before Israel's Supreme Court.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Taliban forces fired back across the Pakistani border for the first time, three days after Pakistan struck seven militant camps inside Afghanistan.</s>
<s>Pakistan has no functioning diplomatic channel to Kabul, and is simultaneously managing a stock market crash, a wave of terror attacks in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈkaɪ.bɚ pækˈtʊŋ.kwɑ">Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</phoneme>, and now this direct military exchange with its neighbor to the west.</s>
<s>Three simultaneous crises, and no line of communication to the one that fired back.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Four former Russian soldiers told the BBC that commanders shot troops at point-blank range for refusing human-wave assaults — attacks designed to trade lives for meters of frozen ground.</s>
<s>Of seventy-nine soldiers mobilized from a single unit, one survived.</s>
<s>Moscow denied the accounts; the men remain wanted fugitives for fleeing a war they say executes its own.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Forces from the Democratic Republic of Congo killed the M-23 rebel movement's spokesman by drone, and struck three further rebel positions across <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɑˈleɪ.heɪ">Kalehe</phoneme> the same morning.</s>
<s>The M-23, which United Nations experts say is backed by Rwanda, controls the coltan mine at <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ruːˈbɑɪ.jɑ">Rubaya</phoneme> — source of roughly fifteen percent of the world's tantalum, the mineral inside every smartphone on earth.</s>
<s>This strike marks a widening offensive against a group that has held vast swathes of eastern Congo for years.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Japan announced it will deploy missiles on <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="joʊ.nɑˈɡuː.ni">Yonaguni</phoneme> island — one hundred and ten kilometers from Taiwan — by 2031, the country's most explicit contingency preparation for conflict in the strait to date.</s>
<s>Defense Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="koʊˈiː.zuː.mi">Koizumi</phoneme> set the timeline for an island community of seventeen hundred people, deepening a military build-up that has doubled Japan's defense spending since 2022.</s>
<s>Beijing restricted exports to twenty Japanese firms the day before the announcement, and has not yet commented on the missiles.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>America's resettlement backlog for Afghan allies would take one hundred and seventy-three years to clear.</s>
<s>One hundred and eighty thousand Afghans who aided United States forces are stranded after a January 2025 refugee ban froze all processing — and by March thirty-first, when the last transit camp in Qatar closes, Washington is offering each person four thousand five hundred dollars to abandon their claim.</s>
<s>No legal challenge has yet halted the camp closure.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At the International Criminal Court, prosecutors presented evidence that Philippine police strangled children with packing tape and played video of former president Rodrigo <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="duːˈtɛr.teɪ">Duterte</phoneme> declaring: I am the sole person responsible.</s>
<s>The charges before the court cover seventy-six killings; rights groups estimate the drug war took up to thirty thousand lives.</s>
<s>Whether international justice can reach a former leader who still commands significant domestic support is the deeper question this case will pose.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The United States Federal Trade Commission found that Amazon operated a secret algorithm called Project Nessie that signaled competitors to raise prices in lockstep, generating one billion dollars in excess profit while inflating costs across the broader economy.</s>
<s>Seventeen state attorneys general have joined the federal case, which goes to trial in October 2026.</s>
<s>The proceedings may produce the first judicial ruling on whether a dominant marketplace can be held liable for price effects that reach beyond its own platform.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Stripe is reportedly in early talks to acquire PayPal, a company whose stock has fallen eighty percent since 2021, putting the once-dominant payments giant within reach of a private rival now valued at one hundred and fifty-nine billion dollars.</s>
<s>If completed, the deal would merge two of the world's largest payment processors under a single roof.</s>
<s>No agreement has been reached, and PayPal has not confirmed the discussions.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Landslides killed twenty-eight people across <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌmiː.nəs ʒɪˈraɪs">Minas Gerais</phoneme>, Brazil, after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʒuːˈiːz dʒi ˈfɔː.rɑ">Juiz de Fora</phoneme> recorded its rainiest February on record.</s>
<s>Decades of iron ore extraction stripped hillsides bare across the state — the same structural fragility that produced the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="bruː.mɑˈdʒiː.njuː">Brumadinho</phoneme> and Mariana dam disasters — turning this season's rain into mudslides at scale.</s>
<s>Forty people remain missing, and rescue teams warn the rains have not stopped.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Scientists at Peking University have built a transistor gate just one nanometre across — the smallest ever recorded — using a ferroelectric design that computes and stores data in a single component at one-tenth the power consumption of today's chips.</s>
<s>The team filed Chinese patents covering the full manufacturing process, sidestepping Western export restrictions aimed at limiting China's access to advanced semiconductor technology.</s>
<s>Whether the design can scale to mass production remains the open question that will determine whether this is a breakthrough or a laboratory result.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The United States Defense Department gave artificial intelligence company Anthropic a Friday deadline: agree to unrestricted military use of its models, or face compulsion under the Defense Production Act, a Cold War-era law that empowers the government to commandeer private industry for national security purposes.</s>
<s>Anthropic has refused to remove its safety restrictions.</s>
<s>If the Pentagon prevails, every artificial intelligence company's safety commitments become subject to government override — a precedent the industry has never faced.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Inception Labs, an artificial intelligence startup, released a model that generates over one thousand tokens per second — roughly ten times the speed of leading rivals — by abandoning the word-by-word prediction method that has defined the field since 2017.</s>
<s>Mercury 2 uses diffusion, the same technique behind image generators, refining many words simultaneously rather than one at a time.</s>
<s>At one-quarter the price of Google's Gemini Flash, it challenges the cost assumptions the entire industry has been built on.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We return this evening in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>